Subject: [M156] Defer entry removal until database scan iterator is destroyed

In DatabaseCheckHelper::ScanDatabase(), entries with invalid or missing
backing files were previously removed via RemoveFileInfo() while
iterating over the database. If RemoveFileInfo() encountered an error,
HandleError() could close the underlying database instance while the
iterator was still active.

Best to view this change ignoring all whitespace.

This change
- scopes the iterator so that it is destroyed before any entries are removed.
- collects IDs into a list for deferred deletion.
- clears the helper's database pointer once the iterator is created.

This differs from the AI fix by removing
- validates that non-directory entries have a non-zero ID.

While a reasonable change, this is not part of the security problem and
so to minimize risk, I don't want to end up back-porting this
unnecessary change.

